      "writtenOn": "2023-05-26T01:41:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initially I added the flag because I anticipated lots of different default strategies, e.g. union, intersect, filling-output, etc. and figured kExplicit flag would parallel that.\n\nHowever, it\u0027s starting to look like the cases that could use intersect or first-input only conditionally use those (so explicit bounds are cleaner), and the union-cases from the legacy impl. really are more correctly meant to be desired-output-filling.\n\nI am planning to leave this for now, but once all the image filters are ported over, I will do a consolidation pass on the ShaderFlags that are actually used and the function signature for Builder::add() and Builder::eval().",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 750,
