      "writtenOn": "2023-05-26T01:41:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both the old blend and arithmetic filters had very similar workflows for handling union vs intersect vs fg-only vs bg-only vs empty. They treated the infinite-bounds case as union and relied on onAffectsTransparentBlack() and super-class logic to correct the value reported to the final caller.\n\nI\u0027d like onAffectsTransparentBlack() to go away and bounds queries are the source of truth, so this updated function calls out the infinite bounds cases explicitly.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 341,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 341,
        "endChar": 89
      },
      "revId": "ecafd1fbdd0282a79a84d77dc21d22dd6b8a8306",
